according to Okanagan legend each  colored pool has a unique medical power  there's 365 circled here in this lake  each circle has a different healing  property to it so if you have warts you  might go to one to heal and if you have  a body ache or another ailment you might  go to another among the many unusual  features of this lake is the topography  how it lies in the landscape the key to  this lake is that it's a lake that  really doesn't have any outflow even in  terms of groundwater it's the water that  gets into this thing stays put what's  unusual about this lake is that there  are no streams flowing into it and there  are no streams flowing out of it the  lake lies at the bottom of a sealed  hollow basin normally the water cycle  goes from the hills into streams and  rivers into the ocean but because it's a  closed system in the Canadian Rockies  the meltwater from the snowpack and the  winter runs down the hills picking up  salt all the way into the lagoon but  there's nowhere for the water to go  except for through evaporation when in  high summer most of the water evaporates  it leaves behind Martian style  multicolored intensely saline brine  pools so the reason they're different  colors is because they've got different  concentrations and mixtures of salts  when the water runs off of a particular  part of the hill maybe there's a gypsum  salt and it pulls a lot of that gypsum  salt into one of the ponds and another  part of the hill has a different kind of  mineral salt and that'll pull it into a  different pod the water found in each  pool retains a distinctive mineral  profile some pools coronis learns  contain epsom salts which treat  rheumatism and arthritis for okanagan  healers the color of each pool indicates  which mineral is present First Nations  doctors would have actually used them as  a prescription pad but this isn't the  most surprising thing about spotted Lake  the waters here have among the highest  concentrations of sulfates anywhere in  the world it's like a chunk of Mars has  somehow broken off and traveled 33  million miles and what's exciting is  that scientists believe this Martian  type Lake could contain Martian type  life analysis of water from spotted Lake  revealed that tiny organisms are indeed  living in the pools  it's like Mars has come to earth and in  these weird holes are clues to life on  the Red Planet it's possible that some  kind of life like that might be existing  on Mars which would be an insane  discovery
 

